"name":"Glenn Lazarus","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10831","person_slug":"glenn-lazarus","vote":"no"},{"name":"Glenn Sterle","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10610","person_slug":"glenn-sterle","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ian Macdonald","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10401","person_slug":"ian-macdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Jacqui Lambie","party":"Jacqui Lambie Network","person_id":"tvfy_10830","person_slug":"jacqui-lambie","vote":"no"},{"name":"James McGrath","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10833","person_slug":"james-mcgrath","vote":"no"},{"name":"Jan McLucas","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10447","person_slug":"jan-mclucas","vote":"no"},{"name":"Janet Rice","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10836","person_slug":"janet-rice","vote":"no"},{"name":"Joe Bullock","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10826","person_slug":"joe-bullock","vote":"no"},{"name":"Joe Ludwig","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10397","person_slug":"joe-ludwig","vote":"no"},{"name":"John Madigan","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10759","person_slug":"john-madigan","vote":"no"},{"name":"John Williams","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10716","person_slug":"john-williams","vote":"no"},{"name":"Larissa Waters","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10764","person_slug":"larissa-waters","vote":"no"},{"name":"Lee Rhiannon","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10760","person_slug":"lee-rhiannon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Lisa Singh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10761","person_slug":"lisa-singh","vote":"no"},{"name":"Matthew Canavan","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10827","person_slug":"matthew-canavan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mitch Fifield","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10224","person_slug":"mitch-fifield","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick Xenophon","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10717","person_slug":"nick-xenophon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nova Peris","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10820","person_slug":"nova-peris","vote":"no"},{"name":"Penny Wright","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10765","person_slug":"penny-wright","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ricky Muir","party":"Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party","person_id":"tvfy_10834","person_slug":"ricky-muir","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"no"}],"name":"Regulations and Determinations — Competition and Consumer (Industry Code — Port Terminal Access (Bulk Wheat)) Regulation 2014; Disallowance","noes":42,"question":"David Leyonhjelm I, and also on behalf of Senator Day, move business of the Senate notice of motion No. 1: That the provisions of subclauses 5(1), 5(4) and 5(5) of the Competition and Consumer (Industry Code—Port Terminal Access (Bulk Wheat)) Regulation 2014, as contained in Select Legislative Instrument 2014 No. 136 and made under the Competition and Consumer Act 2010, be disallowed. Acting Deputy President, could I have some guidance as to whether there will be other speakers. Senator Day and I are both ready to speak. I understand there is a right of reply at the end. John Williams Senators Cash, Cameron and Siewert have indicated that they will be speaking to the motion. David Leyonhjelm Thank you. The disallowance motion moved by Senator Day and me will prevent the Minister for Agriculture, Barnaby Joyce, from exempting monopoly grain marketer, CBH, from port access conditions that will apply to other port operators. Passage of this disallowance motion would remove the minister's power to exempt cooperatives from the code. I would make CBH subject to the same conditions as GrainCorp—no more, no less. This would ensure fairness in that the same rules would apply to all who seek access to ports for the export of their grain. The government might mouth words about free markets and capitalism, but in agriculture the lure of agrarian socialism is never far from the surface. Since the end of the single desk, in 2007, various changes to legislation were made that took the wheat export market towards deregulation. We have moved far beyond the old days of the single desk. I support this progress. One of the interim measures in the transition was the adoption of mandatory port access codes for the export of grain. Following the expiry of undertakings to the ACCC last October, access to port services is now governed by the code and general competition law. Adoption of the code last year was seen by the government as: … a significant step towards free and open competition ","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3708","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-03-04/2"}
